From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:34:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Matchmaker: rematch cooldown for solo rooms, ROOM-END /
 ROOM-SUMMARY log

LA 2026-11-16: room 19 (mix) was an exact rematch of room 18 (same four node ids, same teams) made
the second the 4th cab re-entered, and two cabs got 21-01 while loading; room 13 (class) repeated
room 12 twenty seconds after its first re-entry, no result. Every other solo rematch in the VPS
history formed 39 s or more after the first re-entry and played.

OnlineMatching.RematchCooldownSeconds (default 30, 0 = off): nodes whose last room is the same
humans-vs-humans room are kept out of a solo-entry room together until N s after that room's first
re-entry. Rooms with a team entry, CPU / lone-team / pair rooms and pair worlds are unchanged, so
continue-pair, after-CPU and the regroup rooms behave as before. Logs REMATCH-COOLDOWN defer/placed.

OnlineMatching.LogRoomEnd (default on) + RoomEndTimeoutSeconds (900): ROOM-END per cab after a match
(reentry / reentry-new-node / cancel-after-match / cancel / timeout, seconds since the match, when it
fetched the room) and ROOM-SUMMARY once all cabs are accounted for. The MMS protocol carries no
UDPHP / RTT result, so this is what the matchmaker can see.

Tests: RematchCooldownTests (15). Matchmaking.Tests 435/435; with the production defaults forced on,
every older scenario still passes.

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
