 * `false` = pre-v11 behaviour. Tests: `Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/NoCpuPartnerTests.cs`.
 
+## Rematch cooldown and ROOM-END log (2026-11-16)
+21-01 on four cabs on one LAN: room 19 (Mix) was an exact rematch of room 18 (same four node ids, same teams), made the
+second the 4th cab re-entered (0 s after that room's first re-entry, ~27 s after its results), and two cabs got 21-01 while
+loading. Room 13 (Class) was the same for room 12 (20 s after the first re-entry), no result saved. In the matchmaker's
+history every other solo rematch formed 39 s or more after the first re-entry and played.
+
+* `OnlineMatching.RematchCooldownSeconds` (default **30**, 0 = off): two nodes whose last room is the same
+  humans-vs-humans room are not placed in a room made only of solo entries until this many seconds after that room's
+  first re-entry (the first EntryMatching of any of its nodes). Other cabs still match at once; after the cooldown the
+  same group may meet again. Rooms with a team entry (continued duo regrouping with its former opponents, after-CPU duo,
+  cross-world), earlier humans-vs-CPU / lone-team / pair rooms, and pair worlds are unchanged.
+  Log: `REMATCH-COOLDOWN defer <world> nodes=[..] room=N pairs=[a+b,..] left=Ns`, then `REMATCH-COOLDOWN placed room=M`.
+* `OnlineMatching.LogRoomEnd` (default on), `RoomEndTimeoutSeconds` (900): per cab after a match,
+  `ROOM-END room=N <world> node=X serial=.. reason=reentry|reentry-new-node|cancel-after-match|cancel|timeout +Ns since
+  match fetched=+Ns|never order=k/n`, and once every cab is accounted for
+  `ROOM-SUMMARY room=N .. spread=Ns ends: node:reason@+Ns(fetch ..) ..` (earliest first). A cab that comes back ~100 s
+  after its match while the others come back ~180 s+ or never is the one that dropped. The MMS protocol carries no
+  UDPHP / RTT result (that goes to the card server's CheckCommunication), so these lines are what the matchmaker sees.
+
 ## SoftWait and full 4-human rooms (v12, 2026-11-15)
 `SoftAttributeWaitSeconds` (default 15) still keeps different Mix veteran flags / free-battle win-rate buckets apart at first, so a same-flag 4-human room can still form if more players arrive. A complete 4-human room no longer waits for SoftWait: if a same-flag 4 is not already waiting, a mixed 4 (for example a Teamplay duo + 2 solos with different veteran flags) starts immediately. SoftWait still applies to short-handed rooms (when `NoCpuPartner` is off). Tested 2026-11-15 03:13 PT: a duo + 2 solos used to wait ~14–16 s; they now match at once. 5 new tests (150 total).
 
